    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The United States Geological Survey (USGS) acquired the license to 30 regional\r\nsingle-fold seismic lines in western and central West Virginia in support of ongoing\r\nstructural and stratigraphic framework studies and energy assessments in the central\r\nAppalachians. This report illustrates single-fold seismic reflection data and associated\r\nsupport information. The locations of these regional lines form an irregular grid,\r\ngenerally mimicking drainage topography, which cover portions of western and central\r\nWest Virginia.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
